# Origin of the inference backend (backend/server.py).
#
# Leave UNSET for local dev — vite.config.js's server.proxy already
# forwards the relative /api/* paths to http://localhost:8000, which is
# where `npm run dev:api` serves the backend. Setting this variable in dev
# is unnecessary and would just bypass that proxy.
#
# Required for a deployed build (e.g. on Vercel): that proxy is a Vite
# dev-server feature only and does nothing for `vite build` output, so a
# deployed frontend has no way to reach the backend unless this is set —
# see src/constants/constants.js's API_BASE_URL. Set it in the hosting
# provider's environment variables (e.g. Vercel Project Settings →
# Environment Variables), not in a committed file, to whatever public origin
# is currently serving backend/server.py — for example a Cloudflare Tunnel
# URL while testing on a laptop:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://some-random-words.trycloudflare.com
#
# No trailing slash needed (one is stripped automatically if present).
# Changing this value requires a fresh build/redeploy — Vite inlines
# import.meta.env.* at build time, so it won't take effect on a mere page
# refresh of an already-built bundle.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
